{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CORVO AREA (Corvo addition)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Says whether an address belongs to an area of the site that is switched off.

Three areas can be switched off in the theme settings ("Corvo: areas of the site"): Designers, Portfolio (with the
page of each project) and Tailor your rug (with the TAILOR-MADE rug). While an area is off, nothing on the site leads
to it: its links leave the menus, its buttons give way to the contact button of the settings, its sections are not
drawn, and its own pages say that they are not available (layout/theme.liquid).

Prints the name of the area ("designers", "projects" or "tailor") when the address belongs to an area that is off,
and nothing otherwise.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* url: the address to check, such as the link of a menu or of a button
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign area_url = url | default: '' | downcase
  assign area_off = ''

  if area_url != ''
    if settings.area_tailor == false
      if area_url contains '/pages/tailor-your-rug' or area_url contains '/products/tailor-made'
        assign area_off = 'tailor'
      endif
    endif

    if settings.area_designers == false
      if area_url contains '/pages/designers'
        assign area_off = 'designers'
      endif
    endif

    if settings.area_projects == false
      if area_url contains '/pages/portfolio' or area_url contains '/pages/projects'
        assign area_off = 'projects'
      endif
    endif
  endif

  echo area_off
-%}
